Source: pg-partman
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-all (>= 217~)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/pgpartman/pg_partman

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-partman
Architecture: any
Provides: postgresql-PGVERSION-pg-partman, postgresql-pg-partman
Conflicts: postgresql-PGVERSION-pg-partman
Replaces: postgresql-PGVERSION-pg-partman
Depends: ${postgresql:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, python3:any, python3-psycopg2
Description: Partition management extension for PostgreSQL
 pg_partman creates and manages time-based and number-based table partition
 sets. Native partitioning in PostgreSQL 14+ is supported.
 Child table and trigger function creation is managed by the extension itself.
